WEBVTT

00:29:28.454 --> 00:29:32.829
you're more likely to see first person
plural pronouns like we us.

00:29:33.746 --> 00:29:35.496
Whereas in really good economic times,

00:29:35.496 --> 00:29:39.746
you see a lot of first person
pronouns like me,

00:29:39.746 --> 00:29:45.038
mine I when you think of what's often
called the greatest generation,

00:29:45.579 --> 00:29:48.996
the generation that came of age either in
the Great Depression or World War Two,

00:29:49.454 --> 00:29:51.413
it's been argued again and
again that this is

00:29:51.413 --> 00:29:53.204
the most civically minded generation.

00:29:53.663 --> 00:29:58.204
I do think we will see that going forward
in the current generation.

00:29:58.621 --> 00:30:02.663
Another way, Emily measured individualism
was by looking at Social Security data